`bmb check` does not report the diagnostic E0601 yet: function requires an `#[effects(..)]` attribute. It came with the commit "compiler: M1 front end (parse, check, JSONL diagnostics)". Implement it. Examples of what `bmb check` must print (one JSON line per diagnostic; the path in `file` is the one given on the command line), each after the source line it points at:

    pub fn exposed() -> () {}
    {"code": "E0601", "severity": "error", "message": "`exposed` has no `#[effects(..)]` attribute", "file": "err/items.bmb", "line": 16, "col": 9, "end_line": 16, "end_col": 11, "fix": {"message": "add `#[effects(pure)]` above the function", "replacement": "#[effects(pure)]\nfn"}}

    fn no_effects(x: i64) -> i64 { x }
    {"code": "E0601", "severity": "error", "message": "`no_effects` has no `#[effects(..)]` attribute", "file": "err/rust_habits.bmb", "line": 3, "col": 5, "end_line": 3, "end_col": 7, "fix": {"message": "add `#[effects(pure)]` above the function", "replacement": "#[effects(pure)]\nfn"}}

Everything else the program prints must stay as it is.

